# IMPLEMENTATION_STEPS: cu-002

1. Create pipelines/enrichment/src/test/scala/newspipe/OpenCodeTimeoutSpec.scala with exactly the content in the scala fence below. The stub tree is sh plus sleep, which exists on this box. The polling loop waits up to 5 s for the child to appear so the kill assertion never races process startup.
```scala
package newspipe

import newspipe.infrastructure.llmdataenricher.OpenCodeCliClient
import org.scalatest.funspec.AnyFunSpec
import org.scalatest.matchers.should.Matchers

class OpenCodeTimeoutSpec extends AnyFunSpec with Matchers:
  describe("OpenCodeCliClient.killTree") {
    it("destroys the wrapper and all descendants") {
      val proc = new ProcessBuilder("sh", "-c", "sleep 120").start()
      val deadline = System.currentTimeMillis() + 5000L
      while proc.descendants().count() == 0L && System.currentTimeMillis() < deadline do Thread.sleep(50)
      proc.descendants().count() should be >= 1L
      OpenCodeCliClient.killTree(proc)
      proc.isAlive shouldBe false
      proc.descendants().count() shouldBe 0L
    }

    it("reaps the tree within a bounded time") {
      val proc = new ProcessBuilder("sh", "-c", "sleep 120").start()
      val startNanos = System.nanoTime()
      OpenCodeCliClient.killTree(proc)
      val elapsedMillis = (System.nanoTime() - startNanos) / 1000000L
      elapsedMillis should be < 15000L
    }
  }
```
Prove: `grep -n 'destroys the wrapper' pipelines/enrichment/src/test/scala/newspipe/OpenCodeTimeoutSpec.scala` prints the test line.
2. Run the focused spec, then the whole suite, both from the enrichment pipeline root.
Prove: `sbt "testOnly newspipe.OpenCodeTimeoutSpec"` reports both tests succeeded with workdir pipelines/enrichment.
Prove: `sbt test` passes all suites with workdir pipelines/enrichment.
Do NOT touch: pipelines/enrichment/src/main, pipelines/enrichment/src/test/scala/newspipe/OpenCodeParserSpec.scala, pipelines/enrichment/src/test/scala/newspipe/MergeBackfillSpec.scala, pipelines/enrichment/src/test/scala/newspipe/ConsumerPropsSpec.scala, pipelines/ingestion, build.sbt, .LLMDD.
Stop when the spec exists exactly as fenced and sbt test passes inside pipelines/enrichment. Timeout tuning beyond the 15 s test bound belongs to no other CU; this feature is complete.
